  "notes": "A versatile word with different nuances depending on context and intonation.\n\nUSAGE 1 - HESITATION/MODESTY:\n・まあ、いいでしょう (Well, that should be fine)\n・まあ、そうですね (Well, I suppose so)\n・まあ、{大丈夫|だいじょうぶ}だろう (Well, it'll probably be okay)\n\nUSAGE 2 - SURPRISE (feminine):\n・まあ、{素敵|すてき}！(Oh my, how lovely!)\n・まあ、{大変|たいへん}！(Oh dear!)\n\nUSAGE 3 - SO-SO:\n・まあまあ (so-so, not bad)\n・まあまあ{美味|おい}しい (fairly good)\n\nUSAGE 4 - CALMING:\n・まあまあ、{落|お}ち{着|つ}いて (Now, now, calm down)",
